# Revisions to skip when running `git blame`.
#
# Enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# List only commits that are mechanical across many files — a line-ending sweep,
# a formatter rollout, a mass rename — where the commit's author is never the
# answer to "who wrote this line". One full 40-character SHA per line, with a
# comment above it saying what it did. Never list a commit that changed
# behaviour: blame would then hide the change that matters.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Introducing .gitattributes (PR: codex/gitattributes-normalize) added no entry
# here on purpose. The repository's text blobs were already LF — all 878 of them
# — so `git add --renormalize .` staged nothing and there was no mechanical
# commit to ignore. The sweep changed only how files materialize in a working
# tree (870 files CRLF -> LF on disk), which git blame never sees. This file
# exists so the convention and the config line are in place before the first
# sweep that does rewrite blobs.
